invariant: INV-16
file: src/p256_wide_point.c
catches: diff_p256_wide
reason: the Jacobian doubling writes the database's Z3 = 2 Y1 Z1 beside
  an X3 and a Y3 that are scaled by 1/2 (docs/decisions.md 196). The
  three coordinates then hold another point. The differential compares
  each coordinate with the Lean doubling, which is proven to double.

--- old
    p256_wide_fe_mul(&z3, &a->y, &a->z);
    p256_wide_fe_sqr(&x3, &m);
--- new
    p256_wide_fe_mul(&z3, &a->y, &a->z);
    p256_wide_fe_add(&z3, &z3, &z3);
    p256_wide_fe_sqr(&x3, &m);
